# Line-ending policy — see docs/02-adr/004-line-ending-policy.md
#
# Every file in the initial upload arrived with CRLF, which left scripts/verify.sh
# unparsable by bash ("syntax error: unexpected end of file"). The alpha-spec.md 8.11
# canonical Linux verification command could not run at all.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: shell scripts, where CRLF is FATAL. A blanket
# `* text=auto` would renormalize Cargo.toml, the justfile and the docs on their next
# edit, turning one-line changes into whole-file rewrites and destroying the review
# trail that ADR-001 D5 depends on. Repo-wide normalization is deferred to P1-11.

*.sh            text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-native and its committed bytes are already CRLF. Marked -text so git
# stores them verbatim: `text eol=crlf` would normalize the INDEX to LF, rewriting every line
# of scripts/verify.ps1 in the diff for no functional gain (same reasoning as ADR-004's
# rejection of blanket normalization). P1-11 may normalize deliberately.
*.ps1           -text

# Generated artifacts — reviewers see them collapsed, and never hand-edit them.
.sqlx/**        linguist-generated=true
Cargo.lock      linguist-generated=true
